WEBVTT

00:00:02.439 --> 00:00:07.690
<v Priya Raman>Morning, everyone. Can you hear me, or am I doing the silent Teams presentation again?</v>

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:13.140
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, you're there. Bit tinny, but that's probably this headset.</v>

00:00:15.339 --> 00:00:20.239
<v Hannah Price>Better than the broken coffee machine in the canteen. It's just dispensing disappointment now.</v>

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:24.579
<v Jamie Brennan>So no change in flavour, then.</v>

00:00:25.809 --> 00:00:31.410
<v Hannah Price>At least the disappointment used to be hot. Anyway, that's a moan, not a maintenance request.</v>

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:41.189
<v Priya Raman>I was going to ask about weekend plans, but the weather looks rubbish again. My grand outdoor plans might be the sofa.</v>

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:45.170
<v Marcus Hale>Very sensible. Waterproof sofa, ideally.</v>

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:51.939
<v Priya Raman>Right, Tuesday the twelfth. Let's do the closed stuff first so we don't accidentally give it out again.</v>

00:00:52.880 --> 00:01:00.229
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, so, tested the big boiler yesterday and it's all fine now. That's finished, not another test going on today's list.</v>

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:04.959
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, understood. Good to have that one off the board.</v>

00:01:06.519 --> 00:01:13.170
<v Hannah Price>And I've signed off the inspection on the stretch wrapper on Tuesday — this morning, I mean. That's done.</v>

00:01:13.819 --> 00:01:15.019
<v Priya Raman>Lovely. Both closed.</v>

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:23.250
<v Jamie Brennan>I already swapped the filter on the turbine one compressor yesterday as well. Just making that distinction before filters come up.</v>

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:29.489
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, different one from the air compressor. Easy to muddle them when everyone's talking at once.</v>

00:01:29.870 --> 00:01:32.319
<v Jamie Brennan>Exactly. The turbine one compressor job's finished.</v>

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:39.629
<v Tomasz Nowak>I'll swap the filter on the air compressor this afternoon. It's urgent, that one.</v>

00:01:41.109 --> 00:01:45.310
<v Priya Raman>Thanks, Tom. Air compressor, this afternoon, urgent. That's the live filter job.</v>

00:01:47.209 --> 00:01:50.359
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yep, I'll do that one. Not repeating yesterday's work.</v>

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:55.099
<v Marcus Hale>Good distinction. I was halfway through writing the wrong compressor there.</v>

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:04.049
<v Tomasz Nowak>While I'm on, I heard a slight rattle from the Main Water Isolation Valve. Nothing to action yet, just an observation.</v>

00:02:05.299 --> 00:02:09.150
<v Priya Raman>Right, not a job being allocated off the back of that.</v>

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.789
<v Tomasz Nowak>No, exactly. Just saying what I heard.</v>

00:02:16.289 --> 00:02:23.289
<v Hannah Price>Same sort of thing from me: noticed the boiler was running a bit warm on nights, but it settled down.</v>

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:29.270
<v Marcus Hale>Settled, yeah. Not saying we've got an ongoing temperature problem.</v>

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:33.520
<v Priya Raman>Okay, observation only. No extra boiler work from that.</v>

00:02:35.419 --> 00:02:42.069
<v Olumide Adeyemi>The actual blocker is the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the boiler feed pump. Still no confirmation.</v>

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:47.879
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, there's no firm delivery date behind it. Nothing useful to put against it yet.</v>

00:02:49.479 --> 00:02:54.729
<v Olumide Adeyemi>So that remains blocked. I'm not calling it something we can get on with today.</v>

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:56.840
<v Priya Raman>Understood. Blocked, no new allocation.</v>

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:05.800
<v Tomasz Nowak>Oh, and we were going to replace the belt on the line 2 guard, but that's been pushed to next month, so ignore it.</v>

00:03:07.219 --> 00:03:11.770
