00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:33.170
<v Priya Raman>Exactly. Just the risk assessment update for work on the GT2 water valve.</v>

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:41.209
<v Priya Raman>Han, separate one: can you take vibration readings on the gas turbine one by the 28th? Whenever you get a chance.</v>

00:04:42.889 --> 00:04:48.490
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, that window works. I'll take vibration readings on the gas turbine one by the 28th.</v>

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:54.250
<v Marcus Hale>Gas turbine one itself, yeah? Not that compressor filter we were just talking about.</v>

00:04:55.540 --> 00:05:01.490
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, gas turbine one. Readings, not a filter change. Whenever I get a chance within that deadline.</v>

00:05:02.439 --> 00:05:06.290
<v Priya Raman>Spot on. No need to treat that as an urgent one.</v>

00:05:06.629 --> 00:05:10.829
<v Priya Raman>Fiona, can you organise the toolbox talk for the team for tomorrow?</v>

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:15.209
<v Fiona Doyle>Yes, I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team for tomorrow.</v>

00:05:17.269 --> 00:05:20.069
<v Jamie Brennan>Sorry, you clipped there — tomorrow, not today?</v>

00:05:21.579 --> 00:05:23.680
<v Fiona Doyle>Tomorrow, yeah. That's what I've accepted.</v>

00:05:24.629 --> 00:05:29.180
<v Priya Raman>Right, quick check of the live actions, then we're out of your headphones.</v>

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:38.519
<v Tomasz Nowak>Mine's the air compressor filter, this afternoon. Urgent. The rattle isn't a job, and the line 2 guard belt is deferred.</v>

00:05:40.899 --> 00:05:47.199
<v Jamie Brennan>I've got the near miss at the forklifts write-up, by Wednesday, getting onto it straight away. Safety critical.</v>

00:05:49.689 --> 00:05:57.389
